COMMON:0000190": {"L": "epithelial cell", "T": "class", "P": [], "R": ["Epcam", "Cdh1", "Krt8"], "S": ["Krt7"], "N": ["Vim", "Ptprc", "Pecam1", "Cdh2"], "D": null, "DF": ["Krt18"], "A": [], "MP": [], "GM": {"Krt18": ["11514590", "23449973"], "Epcam": ["32507912", "17600130"], "Krt8": ["24086449", "11514590"], "Cdh1": ["38608805"]}, "GEN": 1}, "MOUSE_COMMON:0000093": {"L": "luminal secretory cell", "T": "class", "P": ["MOUSE_COMMON:0000190"], "R": ["Psca", "Kit"], "S": [], "N": [], "D": null, "DF": ["Elf5"], "A": [], "MP": [], "GM": {"Elf5": ["18316476"], "Psca": ["32807988"], "Kit": ["25803307", "21765473"]}, "GEN": 1}, "MOUSE_COMMON:0000271": {"L": "pigment cell", "T": "class", "P": [], "R": ["Mitf"], "S": [], "N": ["Cd3e"], "D": null, "DF": ["Tyrp1", "Pmel", "Tyr", "Dct", "Mlana"], "A": [], "MP": [], "GM": {"Tyrp1": ["29496358", "31705956"], "Pmel": ["11041368", "23754390"], "Tyr": ["29496358", "31705956"], "Dct": ["9199364"], "Mitf": ["29496358", "31705956"], "Mlana": ["29496358"]}, "GEN": 1}}, "cp": [["luminal progenitor (MOUSE_BREAST:0000002) vs secretory alveolar differentiated (MOUSE_BREAST:0000004)", [], ["Milk proteins Csn2, Wap, Lalba: strongly expressed in Avd (0000004); near-zero in Lp (0000002). A single high-AUC milk-protein required marker forces the Avd call.", "Aldh1a3 and Cd14 (progenitor markers): enriched in Lp, moderately retained in Avd. Not a discriminator alone.", "Developmental context: Avd is abundant only in gestation/lactation or in BRCA1-mutant nulliparous mice (Bach 2021). In WT virgin glands, milk-protein-positive clusters are most likely the lactation-progenitor subset of Lp, not mature Avd.", "Beware the lactation-induced macrophage (0000014), which ALSO expresses Csn2/Csn3/Wap transcripts but is Ptprc+/Cd68+/Itgax+ immune, NOT epithelial. A milk-protein+ cluster that is also Ptprc+/Csf1r+ is liMac, not Avd."]], ["myoepithelial cell (MOUSE_BREAST:0000003) vs pericyte (MOUSE_BREAST:0000010) vs contractile peri-TEB fibroblast (MOUSE_BREAST:0000018)", [], ["Krt14, Krt5, Trp63, Oxtr: strongly positive in myoepithelium (epithelial lineage); absent in pericytes and contractile fibroblasts.", "Rgs5, Pdgfrb, Notch3, Mcam: positive in pericytes (mural); absent/low in myoepithelium and contractile fibroblasts.", "Pdgfra, Vim, Col1a1: positive in contractile peri-TEB fibroblast (fibroblastic); Pdgfra is NEGATIVE in both myoepithelium and pericytes, so Pdgfra+/Acta2+ -> contractile fibroblast.", "Epcam: positive in myoepithelium, negative in pericytes and fibroblasts.", "Entpd1 (CD39)+/CD34-: marks the peri-TEB contractile fibroblast specifically (Sumbal 2025); context = pubertal TEB stroma."]], ["hormone-sensing luminal cell (MOUSE_BREAST:0000001) vs HS-AV hybrid (MOUSE_BREAST:0000006)", [], ["Kit and Elf5 in an Esr1+/Pgr+ cluster: both clearly positive -> HS-AV hybrid. Both near-zero -> pure HS.", "Aldh1a3 in an Esr1+ cluster: positive indicates HS-AV.", "Patel 2023 mammokine signature: Nrg4/Cp enriched in luminal-HS-AV vs HS (which is Adropin/Lrg1-leaning) and AV (Lcn2/Ltf-leaning).", "Gray 2023 caution: HS heterogeneity itself (HS1 vs HS2, the latter Cd200/Prom1/Alcam-high) is NOT the HS-AV hybrid; HS2 still lacks Kit/Elf5. Do not call HS-AV on Cd200/Prom1 alone.", "Size/prevalence: HS-AV is rare (~11% epithelium in young virgin, 0.3% aged). A large Esr1+ cluster without Kit/Elf5 is pure HS."]], ["stromal/perivascular macrophage Mphi1 (MOUSE_BREAST:0000011) vs ductal macrophage Mphi2 (MOUSE_BREAST:0000012) vs lactation-induced macrophage liMac (MOUSE_BREAST:0000014)", [], ["Lyve1 + Mrc1/Cd206 + Folr2: positive in Mphi1 (stromal/perivascular), negative in Mphi2 and liMac.", "H2-Ab1 + Cd74 (MHC-II): positive in Mphi2 (ductal) AND liMac, negative/low in Mphi1. MHC-II alone does NOT separate ductal from liMac.", "Itgax (CD11c) + Clec7a (Dectin-1) + Cx3cr1-hi: positive in liMac, negative in steady-state Mphi2. Clec7a is the most specific liMac marker.", "Itgam (CD11b): negative in liMac, variable in resident subsets.", "Context: liMac is essentially absent in virgin glands and dominates during lactation (peaks ~day 12 pp), resides inside/adjacent to alveoli, and expresses milk-protein transcripts (Csn2/Wap). Mphi1/Mphi2 are present pregestationally.", "Proportional shift with age: Mphi1 (fetal-derived) dominates young glands; Mphi2 (adult BM-derived) and M2-like expand with age (Angarola 2024)."]], ["basal/myoepithelial (MOUSE_BREAST:0000003) vs luminal (hormone-sensing 0000001 / progenitor 0000002)", [], ["Krt14, Krt5, Acta2, Trp63, Oxtr: basal/myoepithelial-defining; absent in luminal cells.", "Krt8, Krt18: luminal-defining; basal cells are Krt8-low/negative.", "Within luminal: Esr1/Pgr/Prlr -> hormone-sensing (0000001); Kit/Elf5/Aldh1a3 -> luminal progenitor (0000002).", "Gray 2023 caution: 'basal-like HS cells' reported in some pubertal scRNA-seq co-express HS + low Krt14/SMA; Gray's HS1 explicitly does NOT, so a Krt14-low/Esr1+ cluster should default to HS, not basal. Require clear Krt14/Krt5 AUC for a basal call.", "CD49f (Itga6) protein is basal-high; useful when keratins are off-panel."]], ["myoepithelial/basal bulk (MOUSE_BREAST:0000003) vs Procr+ basal stem subset (MOUSE_BREAST:0000005)", [], ["Procr, Notch3, Zeb2: enriched in the stem subset (0000005); low in bulk myoepithelium.", "Bulk myoepithelium has high Krt14/Krt5/Acta2/Oxtr/Myh11 (contractile, differentiated); the Procr+ subset is proliferative (cell-cycle genes) and comparatively lower in mature contractile markers.", "Tspan8 marks a SEPARATE quiescent basal stem subset (Gray 2023); Tspan8 is a more informative proliferation indicator than Procr. Tspan8+ and Procr+ are largely non-overlapping.", "Spatial: Procr+/CD34-high basal enriched in TEBs (proliferative); CD34-low/CD200-high nipple basal (Bcl11b+) are the high-self-renewal quiescent stem cells (Lin 2025).", "Beware Procr/Cdh5 partial endothelial overlap: require Krt14+ context to keep the call basal."]], ["mammary fibroblast subtypes: mesenchymal progenitor (0000015) vs lobular-like (0000016) vs adipo-regulatory/preadipocyte (0000017) vs contractile peri-TEB (0000018)", [], ["Dpp4 (CD26) + Pi16 + CD34-high: mesenchymal/interstitial progenitor (0000015), located in fat pad septae/reticulum.", "Pparg + Lpl + Dlk1 (Adipoq-negative): adipo-regulatory/preadipocyte (0000017). F3/Cd142 marks the AREG sub-state lining vessels.", "Crabp1 + Gli1 + periductal location, CD34-low: lobular-like/periductal specialized fibroblast (0000016).", "Acta2 + Vim + Entpd1(CD39), CD34-/Dpp4-: contractile peri-TEB fibroblast (0000018), pubertal TEB tips only.", "Adipoq-positive -> mature adipocyte (0000013), NOT a fibroblast subtype.", "Hierarchy/pseudotime (Pascual 2025): progenitors (Dpp4+) are CD34-high and Hedgehog-low; differentiated specialized fibroblasts gain Gli1/Hedgehog activity and lose CD34."]], ["developmental CAF vs dividing CAF (both abbreviated dCAF)", [], "Bartoschek 2018 dCAF = DEVELOPMENTAL CAF (Scrg1/Sox9/Sox10/Mia, EMT-derived); the pre-existing global Concept CELLMAN_CT:0000579 'dividing CAF (dCAF, breast)' means CYCLING CAF (Mki67/Top2a). The abbreviation collides; use Scrg1 vs Mki67 to split."], ["hormone-sensing progenitor vs HS-AV hybrid luminal cell", ["HS-AV hybrid luminal cell", "hormone-sensing progenitor cell"], "Both are Esr1+ Kit+ luminal cells. Bach 2017 Hsp = Esr1/Prlr/Pgr/S100a6/Cited1 + Aldh1a3/Cd14/Kit (Table 1, cluster Hsp-PI); the HS-AV hybrid Term is keyed on Elf5+Kit. Elf5 is the practical discriminator (alveolar programme ON in HS-AV, not required in Hsp)."]], "oq": ["MOUSE_BREAST:0000026", "MOUSE_BREAST:0000027", "MOUSE_BREAST:0000006", "MOUSE_BREAST:0000001", "MOUSE_BREAST:0000002", "MOUSE_BREAST:0000033"], "ca": [{"name": "mammary macrophage niche (ductal-epithelial vs adipose-stromal/perivascular)", "applies_to": ["macrophage"], "poles": [{"pole": "ductal / epithelium-associated", "context_markers": ["Cd74", "H2-Ab1", "Itgax", "Cx3cr1", "Krt8", "Krt18"], "subtypes": {"macrophage": "